From: ScorchDroid <noreply@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] android: the beam events carry what the beams are drawn with

The laser and lightning events (patch 0011) carried a position, an end and a
size, and made their colours up - the port drew both as plain coloured lines,
so nothing else was needed. V4 draws them as upstream does, which needs the
rest of what the client bodies below read:

- the laser's own <color>, which tints its outer tube. The constant here was
  a pale pink; the shipped Laser is red, and nothing was showing that.
- <ringradius>, the size of the textured rings threaded along the beam. Zero
  for most weapons, which is how upstream switches them off. It rides in
  `value`, which is free on a beam.
- <totaltime> for both, which is what each fades over. Without it the
  renderer used short constants and both were gone sooner than upstream
  shows them.
- lightning's colour becomes white, which is what its client body draws.

Fields only; no game logic.

---
diff --git a/src/common/actions/Laser.cpp b/src/common/actions/Laser.cpp
--- a/src/common/actions/Laser.cpp
+++ b/src/common/actions/Laser.cpp
@@ -199,7 +199,20 @@
 		effect.endY = end[1].asFloat();
 		effect.endZ = end[2].asFloat();
 		effect.size = hurtRadius_.asFloat();
-		effect.r = 1.0f; effect.g = 0.85f; effect.b = 0.85f;
+		// V4: the weapon's own colour, which is what the client body tints
+		// its outer tube with - the pale constant here was a stand-in from
+		// when the port drew the beam as a plain line. The shipped Laser is
+		// red; nothing was showing that.
+		effect.r = params_->getColor()[0];
+		effect.g = params_->getColor()[1];
+		effect.b = params_->getColor()[2];
+		// V4: <ringradius>, the size of the textured rings threaded along
+		// the beam every unit of its length. Zero for most weapons, which
+		// is how upstream switches them off. `value` is free on a beam.
+		effect.value = params_->getRingRadius();
+		// V4: the weapon's <totaltime>, which is what the client body below
+		// fades the beam over.
+		effect.life = laserTime_.asFloat();
 		ScorchDroidEffects::push(effect);
 	}
 #endif
diff --git a/src/common/actions/Lightning.cpp b/src/common/actions/Lightning.cpp
--- a/src/common/actions/Lightning.cpp
+++ b/src/common/actions/Lightning.cpp
@@ -160,7 +160,12 @@
 			effect.endY = segment.end[1].asFloat();
 			effect.endZ = segment.end[2].asFloat();
 			effect.size = segment.size.asFloat();
-			effect.r = 0.75f; effect.g = 0.85f; effect.b = 1.0f;
+			// V4: white, as the client body below draws it - the pale blue
+			// here was a stand-in from when the port drew a plain line.
+			effect.r = 1.0f; effect.g = 1.0f; effect.b = 1.0f;
+			// V4: the bolt's own <totaltime>, which the client body fades
+			// every segment over together.
+			effect.life = weapon_->getTotalTime().asFloat();
 			ScorchDroidEffects::push(effect);
 		}
 	}
